% Regression guard for the dump_barloc() global-buffer-overflow (genmidi.c).
% With -c, abc2midi writes in barloc.txt the size of each bar of each track
% of a tune of several tracks, from barloc[], which keeps the first 1024
% bars only.  dump_barloc() used to read barloc[] up to the number of bars
% of the track, past its end for a tune longer than 1024 bars, as these two
% voices of 1040 bars each.  It now stops at 1024 values, while its header
% still gives the number of bars.  Built with the sanitize preset against the
% pre-fix code this input aborts in dump_barloc, and the other builds dump
% more than 1024 values, so the barloc.txt golden fails without the fix.
X:1
T:More than 1024 bars
C:abc2midi test
M:2/4
L:1/4
K:C
V:1
